meta {
  name: Call Signaling (WebSocket)
  type: ws
  seq: 1
  tags: [
    ws
  ]
}

ws {
  url: ws://localhost:8000/api/v1/ws/appointments/{{appt_id}}/call
  auth: none
}

body:ws {
  name: auth
  type: json
  content: '''
    {"type": "auth", "token": "{{access_token}}"}
  '''
  selected: true
}

docs {
  WebRTC signaling for one appointment (M7). First frame: {"type": "auth", "token": "<jwt>"};
  the server replies {"type": "joined", "device_id", "peer_id"}. Then send
  {"type": "offer" | "answer" | "candidate" | "hangup", "sdp": ..., "call_id": "<uuid>"}.
  The server stamps "from"/"from_device" and always addresses the OTHER participant (no echo);
  frames cross API processes via Redis pub/sub. With several devices, the first answer wins
  (Redis SET NX): later answers get {"type": "error", "code": "ALREADY_ANSWERED"} and the
  callee's other devices get {"type": "answered_elsewhere"}.
  Bruno CLI 4.2 can't run ws; headless check with real WebRTC peers: python scripts/observe_call.py
}
